From: Prarit Bhargava <prarit@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 08:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Default to OpenSSL crypto backend

Match Fedora packaging: use crypto-openssl instead of crypto-nettle.
Hummingbird nettle 4.0 dropped nettle/pgp.h, which breaks nettle-sys
2.3.2 bindgen. OpenSSL is already required at runtime.

Origin: https://src.fedoraproject.org/rpms/rust-rpm-sequoia/blob/rawhide/f/rpm-sequoia-fix-metadata.diff

diff --git a/Cargo.toml b/Cargo.toml
index b28ab141be03..8f23cace3a77 100644
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -42,7 +42,7 @@ crate-type = ["cdylib"]
 
 # We explicitly do not want to enable Sequoia's decompression support.
 # Hence we only select a crypto backend.
-default = ["crypto-nettle"]
+default = ["crypto-openssl"]
 crypto-nettle = ["sequoia-openpgp/crypto-nettle"]
 crypto-rust = ["sequoia-openpgp/crypto-rust"]
 crypto-cng = ["sequoia-openpgp/crypto-cng"]
